t  we all need to go further  spending two percent on defense  must be a floor  not a ceiling  there is no substitute for hard military  power  backed by intelligence and diplomacy  secondly we need to recognize the  growing role the economy plays in  security  in the uk we're now using all of our  economic levers trade sanctions  investment and development policy in a  much more assertive way  we recognize that growth from cheap gas  and money siphoned from kleptocracies  is growth built on sand  it's not the same as real sustained  growth from higher productivity and  greater innovation  free trade and free markets are the most  powerful engine of human progress  we will always champion economic freedom  but free trade must be fair and that  means playing by the rules  for too long many have been naive about  the geopolitical power of economics  aggressors treat it as a tool of foreign  policy  using patronage investment and debt as a  means to exert control and coerce  they're ruthless in their approach  our response won't mirror their malign  tactics but we will match them in our  resolve  it's time to wise up access to the  global economy must depend on playing by  the rules and there can be no more free  passes  we're showing this in the russia ukraine  conflict russia's past has been  rescinded  we're hitting them with every element of  economic policy we've raised tariffs on  russian goods we've cut them off from  wto terms we've banned their ships from  our ports we've banned their planes from  our airports we have sanctioned in the  united kingdom  more individuals and organizations than  any other nation hitting russia's banks  oligarchs defense companies central bank  reserves and oil and gas supplies  we are cutting off the funding for  putin's war effort  we're also cutting investment ties with  russia  banning all new outward investments and  ending the investor visa  at the same time we're removing all  import tariffs for ukraine and we're  supportin