duce strategic  dependence  and we can help each other to weather  the storm  of soaring food and energy prices  at the world bank last week we secured  170 billion dollars to help low-income  countries deal with these challenges  and we're getting ahead in other  possible areas of strategic dependence  whether it's minerals or rare earth  metals we're joining forces to prevent  future problems before they emerge  this is how we will strengthen  our shared economic security  that brings me on to the final point  which is that our prosperity and  security must be built on a network of  strong partnerships  this is what i've described as the  network of liberty  the fundamental principle  is that no matter the challenges we  should not turn inward and pursue  autarky  we should reach out and embrace new  partnerships  what the dutch and others have called  open autonomy  in a world where malign actors are  trying to undermine multilateral  institutions  we know that bilateral and plural actual  groups will play a greater role  partnerships like the nato like the g7  and the commonwealth are vital  and we should keep strengthening our  nato alliance with bonds around the  world  like the uk led joint expeditionary  force the five eyes and the orcas  partnership that we have with united  states and australia  and we want to keep growing our ties  with countries like japan  india and indonesia  we also should build on the strong core  that we have in the g7  during the uk's presidency last year i  was pleased to bring friends like  australia korea india south africa and  asean to the table  the g7 should act as an economic nato  collectively defending our prosperity  if the economy of a partner is being  targeted by an aggressive regime we  should act to support them  all for one and one for all  and to the 141 countries from all  continents who voted to condemn russia's  action at the un  i hear your voice  i share your outrage at russia's illegal  war  and i share your fundamental belief  in sovereignty in fair play and the rule  of law  so let's work together  let's forge deeper bonds let's be better  traders investors and partners than the  aggressors  the uk is prepared to do things  differently we're prepared to think  differently and we're prepared to work  differently with you to get things done  there is huge strengths in collective  action  and let me be clear this also applies to  alliances that the uk is not part of  we support the indo-pacific quad  we support an outward-looking eu and  we're working closely together on  ukraine  we support asean the african union and  the u.s mexico canada trade agreement  we reject the old ideas of hierarchical  systems exclusive groups and spheres of  influence  we want to see a network of partnerships  stretching around the world standing up  for sovereignty and self-determination  and building shared prosperity and the  uk  will be an active and agile part of this  network  actually excellencies ladies and  gentlemen  geopolitics is back  after the cold war  we all thought that peace stability and  prosperity would spread inexorably  around the globe  we thought that we learnt the lessons of  history and the march of progress would  continue unchallenged  we were wrong  but this is no council of despair  in the face of rising aggression we do  have the power to act and we need to act  now  we must be assertive  aggressors are looking at what has  happened in ukraine and we need to make  sure that they get the right message  together we have tremendous strength  let's use it to forge a better more  secure world and a stronger global  economy  this will take the energies of all of  the people in this room and beyond  it will be hard  but we have to step up and take  responsibility  the aggressors are prepared to be bold  we must be bolder  that is how we will ensure that  ukraine's sovereignty is restored  that is how we will ensure  that aggression and coercion fail  and that is how  across the globe  we will win this new era for peace  security and prosperity  thank you  now ladies and gentlemen i invite you to  join me in a toast to thank our host for  this evening  the lord mayor and the lady may arrest  [Applause]  you

